+ * Both arrive on the entry's `_meta.claudeCode` — the same vendor corner this
+ * adapter already uses for `backgroundTask` — and only when they were actually
+ * read: a session whose transcript could not be scanned keeps its protocol
+ * fields and says nothing here, rather than costing the whole list.
+ *
+ * `messageCount` is the SDK's own definition of a session's messages
+ * (`getSessionMessages().length`, with the harness's meta rows already out of
+ * it), not a line or byte count: the cheap versions measure the wrong thing on
+ * a real transcript — a coding conversation's own CONTENT quotes
+ * `"type":"user"` markers too often for substring counting to survive
+ * (measured 4x the true count on a 26 MB corpus).
+ *
+ * A read is memoized by the SDK record's own `(fileSize, lastModified)`, which
+ * move exactly when the transcript does — so a repeated `session/list` pays
+ * the full parse only for the conversations that moved since the last one.
